  "details": "When using VRChat in desktop mode and leaving the application running while AFK (e.g., during work or long idle periods), real-time rendering continues unnecessarily. This results in wasted system resources, increased power consumption, and louder fan noise.\n\nI propose an optional feature that reduces rendering frequency while in AFK mode on desktop. For example, rendering could update only every 30 seconds or 1 minute when AFK is detected. An optional on-screen indicator could show when this low-power mode is active (with the ability to hide it if desired).\n\nThis feature should be enabled by default but allow users to disable it in settings for those who prefer full rendering at all times. It would significantly reduce resource usage and improve user experience during idle periods.",
